#: ../../source/fastq_README.md:148
msgid "<a name=\"fastqueue\"></a>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fastq_README.md:149
msgid "fastqueue([that], worker, concurrency)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fastq_README.md:151
msgid "Creates a new queue."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fastq_README.md:153 ../../source/fastq_README.md:274
msgid "Arguments:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fastq_README.md:155 ../../source/fastq_README.md:275
msgid "`that`, optional context of the `worker` function."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fastq_README.md:156
msgid ""
"`worker`, worker function, it would be called with `that` as `this`, if "
"that is specified."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fastq_README.md:158 ../../source/fastq_README.md:278
msgid ""
"`concurrency`, number of concurrent tasks that could be executed in "
"parallel."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fastq_README.md:162
msgid "<a name=\"push\"></a>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fastq_README.md:163
msgid "queue.push(task, done)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fastq_README.md:165
msgid ""
"Add a task at the end of the queue. `done(err, result)` will be called "
"when the task was processed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fastq_README.md:169
msgid "<a name=\"unshift\"></a>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fastq_README.md:170
msgid "queue.unshift(task, done)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fastq_README.md:172
msgid ""
"Add a task at the beginning of the queue. `done(err, result)` will be "
"called when the task was processed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fastq_README.md:176
msgid "<a name=\"pause\"></a>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fastq_README.md:177
msgid "queue.pause()"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fastq_README.md:179
msgid "Pause the processing of tasks. Currently worked tasks are not stopped."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fastq_README.md:183
msgid "<a name=\"resume\"></a>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fastq_README.md:184
msgid "queue.resume()"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fastq_README.md:186
msgid "Resume the processing of tasks."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fastq_README.md:189
msgid "<a name=\"idle\"></a>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fastq_README.md:190
msgid "queue.idle()"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fastq_README.md:192
msgid ""
"Returns `false` if there are tasks being processed or waiting to be "
"processed. `true` otherwise."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fastq_README.md:196
msgid "<a name=\"length\"></a>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fastq_README.md:197
msgid "queue.length()"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fastq_README.md:199
msgid "Returns the number of tasks waiting to be processed (in the queue)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fastq_README.md:202
msgid "<a name=\"getQueue\"></a>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fastq_README.md:203
msgid "queue.getQueue()"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fastq_README.md:205
msgid ""
"Returns all the tasks be processed (in the queue). Returns empty array "
"when there are no tasks"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fastq_README.md:208
msgid "<a name=\"kill\"></a>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fastq_README.md:209
msgid "queue.kill()"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fastq_README.md:211
msgid ""
"Removes all tasks waiting to be processed, and reset `drain` to an empty "
"function."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fastq_README.md:215
msgid "<a name=\"killAndDrain\"></a>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fastq_README.md:216
msgid "queue.killAndDrain()"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fastq_README.md:218
msgid ""
"Same than `kill` but the `drain` function will be called before reset to "
"empty."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fastq_README.md:221
msgid "<a name=\"error\"></a>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fastq_README.md:222
msgid "queue.error(handler)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fastq_README.md:224
msgid ""
"Set a global error handler. `handler(err, task)` will be called each time"
" a task is completed, `err` will be not null if the task has thrown an "
"error."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fastq_README.md:228
msgid "<a name=\"concurrency\"></a>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fastq_README.md:229
msgid "queue.concurrency"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fastq_README.md:231
msgid ""
"Property that returns the number of concurrent tasks that could be "
"executed in parallel. It can be altered at runtime."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fastq_README.md:235
msgid "<a name=\"paused\"></a>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fastq_README.md:236
msgid "queue.paused"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fastq_README.md:238
msgid ""
"Property (Read-Only) that returns `true` when the queue is in a paused "
"state."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fastq_README.md:241
msgid "<a name=\"drain\"></a>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fastq_README.md:242
msgid "queue.drain"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fastq_README.md:244
msgid ""
"Function that will be called when the last item from the queue has been "
"processed by a worker. It can be altered at runtime."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fastq_README.md:249
msgid "<a name=\"empty\"></a>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fastq_README.md:250
msgid "queue.empty"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fastq_README.md:252
msgid ""
"Function that will be called when the last item from the queue has been "
"assigned to a worker. It can be altered at runtime."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fastq_README.md:257
msgid "<a name=\"saturated\"></a>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fastq_README.md:258
msgid "queue.saturated"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fastq_README.md:260
msgid ""
"Function that will be called when the queue hits the concurrency limit. "
"It can be altered at runtime."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fastq_README.md:265
msgid "<a name=\"promise\"></a>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fastq_README.md:266
msgid "fastqueue.promise([that], worker(arg), concurrency)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fastq_README.md:268
msgid ""
"Creates a new queue with `Promise` apis. It also offers all the methods "
"and properties of the object returned by [`fastqueue`](#fastqueue) with "
"the modified [`push`](#pushPromise) and [`unshift`](#unshiftPromise) "
"methods."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fastq_README.md:272
msgid "Node v10+ is required to use the promisified version."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fastq_README.md:276
msgid ""
"`worker`, worker function, it would be called with `that` as `this`, if "
"that is specified. It MUST return a `Promise`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fastq_README.md:281
msgid "<a name=\"pushPromise\"></a>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fastq_README.md:282
msgid "queue.push(task) => Promise"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fastq_README.md:284
msgid ""
"Add a task at the end of the queue. The returned `Promise`  will be "
"fulfilled (rejected) when the task is completed successfully "
"(unsuccessfully)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fastq_README.md:287 ../../source/fastq_README.md:295
#: ../../source/fastq_README.md:302
msgid ""
"This promise could be ignored as it will not lead to a "
"`'unhandledRejection'`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fastq_README.md:289
msgid "<a name=\"unshiftPromise\"></a>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fastq_README.md:290
msgid "queue.unshift(task) => Promise"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fastq_README.md:292
msgid ""
"Add a task at the beginning of the queue. The returned `Promise`  will be"
" fulfilled (rejected) when the task is completed successfully "
"(unsuccessfully)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fastq_README.md:297
msgid "<a name=\"drained\"></a>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fastq_README.md:298
msgid "queue.drained() => Promise"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fastq_README.md:300
msgid ""
"Wait for the queue to be drained. The returned `Promise` will be resolved"
" when all tasks in the queue have been processed by a worker."
msgstr ""

